{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "note": "The game's design tokens — the registry the world editor builds its theme form from, so adding a token here teaches both sides about it. `css` is the custom property applied to :root and `default` MUST match the value in src/styles.css, which tests/test_theme_tokens.py enforces in both directions.",
  "history": "v1 held NINE tokens while styles.css held 183 colour literals against 34 var() uses — the editor could reach about a sixth of the colour in the game, and --warm and --kola were not used anywhere in src/ at all: two knobs in the form wired to nothing. v2 is the full sweep: every colour and every type stack in the stylesheet now resolves through one of these. The sweep also DELETED --warm and --kola: they had no var() anywhere in src/, so two of the nine knobs the form offered were wired to nothing.",
  "types": {
    "color": "a finished colour value — use it directly",
    "channelRgb": "`r,g,b` WITHOUT the wrapper, for `rgba(var(--x-rgb), α)`. A colour used at a dozen opacities is one colour and a dozen local decisions; the alpha belongs to the rule that chose it, not to the theme.",
    "channelOklch": "`L C H` without the alpha, for `oklch(var(--x-oklch) / α)`. Same idea.",
    "fontStack": "a font-family list, fallbacks included"
  },
